{"id":"~Matteo_Gioia1","name":"Matteo Gioia","counts":{"accepted_papers":1,"first_position_papers":0,"co_first_author_papers":null,"corresponding_author_papers":null,"Poster only":1},"papers":[{"id":"KdaClHHEUt","title":"T-Rex: Tactile-Reactive Dexterous Manipulation","abstract":"The ability to react dynamically to tactile signals has long been considered crucial to agile human-level dexterity. Yet contemporary learning-based VLAs for robotic manipulation generally either overlook the tactile modality or are limited to encoders with static cues, in part due to  the scarcity of diverse training data and standardized evaluation, architectural constraints in current Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models, and limitations of static tactile encoders. In this paper, we push the frontier of tactile-reactive manipulation addressing all of these limitations. We open-source a large-scale, 100-hour tactile-rich dataset collected via a novel, data-efficient recipe that prioritizes elementary motor primitives. To effectively exploit naturally high-frequency touch signals without sacrificing the existing capabilities of existing VLAs, we introduce a variable-rate Mix-of-Transformer (MoT) architecture equipped with a novel temporal tactile VQ-VAE encoder. We demonstrate the effectiveness of tactile-reactive policies on 12 manipulation tasks requiring delicate force control, deformable object manipulation, achieving over 30% higher average success rate than the strongest baseline.","summary":"围绕接触状态快速变化的灵巧操作，将触觉反馈用于反应式动作修正。研究多阶段训练如何帮助策略在手物接触中及时调整，而不只依赖视觉与预定动作。","type":"Poster only","topics":["视觉语言动作与基础模型","数据与评测","触觉与接触","灵巧操作与机器人手"],"title_topics":["触觉与接触","灵巧操作与机器人手"],"authors":["~Dantong_Niu1","~Zhuoyang_Liu1","~Zekai_Wang6","~Boning_Shao1","~Zhao-Heng_Yin1","~Anirudh_Pai1","~Yuvan_Sharma1","~Stefano_Saravalle1","~Ruijie_Zheng1","~Jing_Wang79","~Ryan_Punamiya1","~Mengda_Xu1","~Yuqi_Xie1","~Yunfan_Jiang1","~Letian_Fu1","~Konstantinos_Kallidromitis1","~Matteo_Gioia1","~Junyi_Zhang3",